  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A transmitting antenna at the top of a tower has a height <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>32</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> and the height of the receiving antenna is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>. What is the maximum distance between them for satisfactory communication in line of sight (LOS) mode?</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>45</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>54</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>55</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>455</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given,</p><p>Height of transmitting&nbsp;antenna is,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>h</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math></p><p>Height of receiving antenna is,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>h</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>32</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math></p><p>Thus,&nbsp;maximum distance for satisfactory communication will be,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi><msub><mi>h</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></msub></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi><msub><mi>h</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></msub></msqrt></math>&nbsp;where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;is radius of the Earth,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi><msub><mi>h</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></msub></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi><msub><mi>h</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></msub></msqrt><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><msub><mi>d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>64</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>50</mn></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>64</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>32</mn></msqrt><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><msub><mi>d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>8000</mn><msqrt><mn>10</mn></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>6400</mn><msqrt><mn>10</mn></msqrt><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><msub><mi>d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>14400</mn><msqrt><mn>10</mn></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><msub><mi>d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>45536</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><msub><mi>d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>45</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi></math></p>"
  }
}